## A keepsake with a practical purpose

Bottle opener challenge coins combine double-sided custom artwork with a functional opening point. They suit brewery merchandise, hospitality promotions, unit reunions, club events and company outings where a commemorative piece can remain useful after the occasion.

## Center cutout or edge hook

A center cutout makes the opener an obvious part of the design. An edge hook keeps more of the coin face available for the main emblem. Plan the opening early, leave enough metal around it and balance the remaining artwork across both faces.

For comfortable grip and leverage, a starting size of 2 inches is recommended. A 2.5-3 inch format offers more room for detailed artwork and a larger opening tool. The shape and opener position are reviewed together before tooling.

## Finish and function, designed together

The approved artwork defines the coin and opener before metal forming and tooling. Color can be added to one or both faces, or the design can stay in an antique metal finish. Inspection covers both appearance and opener function before packaging. Choose plating, edge and presentation to suit the intended use, from informal event merchandise to a boxed commemorative gift.

## Plan your order

The minimum order is 50 pieces. Typical production takes 12-18 business days excluding shipping. Send both-face artwork, preferred dimensions, quantity, destination and target date, with a note about the opener style and principal message.
